.TH LUS-COMPLETIONS 1 "" "Lus" "Lus Manual"
.SH NAME
lus-completions \- print a shell completion script
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\fBlus completions\fR bash|zsh|fish|powershell
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Prints the script that completes the commands, options, and arguments of \fBlus\fR in a shell, such as the options of \fBlus test\fR, the formats of \fBlus doc \-\-format\fR, and the permissions after \fB\-P\fR.
The script describes the running \fBlus\fR, so write it again after an upgrade that adds a command or an option.
Each shell reads completions from a place of its own, which the following commands write to.
.TP
\fBbash\fR
\fBlus completions bash > ~/.local/share/bash\-completion/completions/lus\fR, which bash-completion loads the first time \fBlus\fR is completed.
.TP
\fBzsh\fR
\fBlus completions zsh > ~/.zfunc/_lus\fR, with \fBfpath+=~/.zfunc\fR in \fB~/.zshrc\fR before \fBcompinit\fR runs.
.TP
\fBfish\fR
\fBlus completions fish > ~/.config/fish/completions/lus.fish\fR.
.TP
\fBpowershell\fR
\fBlus completions powershell | Out\-String | Invoke\-Expression\fR in the file that \fB$PROFILE\fR names.
.PP
The exit status is 2 when the shell is missing or unknown.
.PP
The release archives carry the same scripts and a man page for \fBlus\fR and for each command, such as \fBlus\-test\fR, under \fBshare\fR, at the paths that Linux distributions and Homebrew install from: \fBshare/man/man1\fR, \fBshare/bash\-completion/completions\fR, \fBshare/zsh/site\-functions\fR, and \fBshare/fish/vendor_completions.d\fR.
\fBzig build install\fR puts the same tree under its prefix, so a package of a distribution copies it unchanged.
The install script unpacks a release into \fB~/.lus/versions/VERSION\fR, so \fBman lus\fR finds the pages once \fBMANPATH\fR names \fB~/.lus/versions/VERSION/share/man\fR.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
0
The script was printed.
.TP
2
The shell is missing or unknown.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR lus (1)
.PP
The CLI page of the Lus manual, https://lus.dev/manual/cli#lus-completions, has the same text with links to the rest of the manual.
